# E §5 step 1, C-4's clause under a `?` law date (tally 2.3, #247; the lead's P8): `at w` with
# `w = ?"which law day?"` keeps the amounts at the booking cut unread, so whether a1 (known 2026-03-20, raising
# `amt`) changes the instance isn't known: a binding over `adjustments` that could hold it is the hole, as under
# the window twin (E5_hole_at_adjustments_count). Before: 0, where every answer to the `?` gives 1.
=== m.tally
model f9q
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input other: money PLN
input w: date
input d_at: date
input dd: date
move pay: transfers
  on dd
  at w
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d_at = 2026-03-01 "s"
  other = 1.00 PLN "s"
  w = ?"which law day?"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
version a0
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  dd = 2026-03-10 "s"
version a1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-20
  replace amt = 150.00 PLN "s"
ask adj: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04)
ask asum: sum(a.change for a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04)
ask k19: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) as known 2026-03-19
ask k20: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) as known 2026-03-20
=== expect
adj: ?"which law day?" (w)
  cut 2026-06-10
asum: ?"which law day?" (w)
  cut 2026-06-10
k19: 0
  cut 2026-03-19
k20: ?"which law day?" (w)
  cut 2026-03-20
warning: WARN-UNREAD input d_at is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input other is read by nothing
